# Architecture Patterns

## Client-Side Application

This is a client-side web application (SPA) optimized for mobile-first design. All calculation logic runs in the browser via WebAssembly.

- **Frontend**: Vue.js/Nuxt.js handles UI and user interactions (mobile-first)
- **Calculations**: Rust compiled to WASM performs all ILR calculations client-side
- **Server**: Lightweight server serves static assets and provides minimal API if needed

## Data Flow

```
User Input (Vue Component)
  ↓
Composable (useAbsenceCalculator)
  ↓
WASM Module (Rust calculation functions)
  ↓
Results (JSON)
  ↓
Display (Vue Component with shadcn/ui)
```

## WASM Integration Strategy

- Load WASM module once on app initialization
- Expose calculation functions through composables
- Keep WASM bundle size minimal (avoid heavy dependencies)
- Handle WASM loading errors gracefully

```typescript
// Load WASM on app init
const wasmModule = await import('@/wasm/ilr_calculator')
// Expose through composable
export const useAbsenceCalculator = () => ({
  calculate: (periods: AbsencePeriod[]) => 
    wasmModule.calculate_rolling_absences(JSON.stringify(periods))
})
```

## Separation of Concerns

- **Rust/WASM**: Pure calculation logic, no UI dependencies
- **Vue Components**: UI rendering, user interaction, form validation
- **Composables**: Bridge between Vue and WASM, handle data transformation
- **Server**: Static file serving, optional API endpoints for future features

## Build and Deployment

- Separate Rust WASM build (`wasm-pack build`)
- Frontend build (Nuxt/Vite)
- Server setup for static hosting (minimal Node.js/Deno server or CDN)

## Performance Considerations

- Lazy load WASM module (don't block initial render)
- Debounce user input for real-time calculations
- Cache calculation results when inputs haven't changed
- Optimize WASM bundle size (tree-shake unused code)
- **Mobile optimization**: Minimize initial bundle size, optimize for slower mobile networks
- **Touch performance**: Ensure smooth interactions on mobile devices
- **Viewport optimization**: Use proper meta tags for mobile viewport (`width=device-width, initial-scale=1`)

## Future Extensibility

Architecture supports adding:
- Server-side API endpoints (e.g., data persistence, user accounts)
- Progressive Web App (PWA) features
- Offline calculation capability (WASM runs offline)
